// Reven — database schema.
//
// See PRD §4.2 and §10.3 module boundaries for the full domain model. Tables
// land incrementally, feature by feature — see docs/ROADMAP.md for order.
// Every future tenant-owned table must carry id (uuid), tenant_id, created_at/by,
// updated_at/by, version and lifecycle status per PRD §4.1 data modeling rules.
//
// Feature: Authentication.
// `User` is deliberately NOT tenant-owned — PRD's entity model treats
// identity and tenant-membership as separate concerns (a person's account vs.
// their role inside a given tenant).
//
// Feature: Tenant / Organization.
// `Membership` is the join between `User` and `Tenant`, carrying the role.
// One user can in principle hold memberships in more than one tenant — the
// schema doesn't forbid it — but this phase only builds the single-tenant
// path (sign up → no membership → create one tenant → done); a tenant
// switcher for a user with several memberships is future work, not
// something this phase's UI handles.
//
// Feature: Roles and Permissions / RBAC (this migration).
// `MembershipRole` grows from a placeholder OWNER/MEMBER to the six tiers in
// PRD §2.3's MVP capability matrix (Owner, Admin, Executive, Manager,
// Reviewer, Guest — Owner and Admin share the "Admin" column there, split
// out because ADM-03's "prevent removal of the final active Tenant Owner"
// invariant needs Owner to be a real, distinct value). Existing MEMBER rows
// migrate to MANAGER — the closest analog to "a regular contributor" in the
// old two-tier model. `Invitation` implements ADM-02 (invite members) for
// the one path this phase builds: a brand-new email with no existing User.
// An email that already has an account gets a conflict on invite — merging
// an invite into an existing account is out of scope for this phase.
//
// Feature: Partner (this migration). First table in the `portfolio` module
// (PRD §10.3) — Phase 2 of docs/ROADMAP.md, ahead of Partnership. Also the
// first table where every PRD §4.1 data-modeling rule actually applies:
// `User`, `Tenant`, `Membership` and `Invitation` each had a reason to skip
// one or more (see their own comments above). `identifiers` is a free-form
// JSON map rather than named columns — PRD §4.2 says only "identifiers"
// (plural), naming no specific scheme, and inventing one (VAT number? DUNS?
// a platform-specific ID?) isn't this phase's call to make; CSV import
// (Roadmap Phase 2, item 6) is what will actually populate it from a real
// source system. `segment` is free text for the same reason — a controlled
// taxonomy is ADM-05 (P1, not built).
//
// Feature: Partnership (this migration). PRD §4.3's Table 13 gives its state
// machine as one arrow-chain: Prospect → Qualified → Planning → Active → At
// Risk → Paused → Terminated → Archived, "cannot activate without owner,
// motion, objective and cadence." Table 67 adds per-field gating: owner_id
// required starting at Qualified (earlier than Active), health and
// next_review_at required starting at Active. None of the PRD's per-object
// tables draw a reverse arrow for ANY object — including ones where recovery
// is obviously required (Initiative's Blocked, Action's Blocked) — so a
// literal forward-only reading would make a governed relationship unable to
// recover from At Risk, which defeats the point of tracking health at all.
// `PartnershipsService.canTransition` therefore implements: strict forward
// order Prospect→Qualified→Planning→Active (no skipping, since `stage`'s own
// validation rule is "valid state transition only"); Active⇄AtRisk⇄Paused as
// a recoverable trio; Terminated reachable from any pre-Archived stage
// (ending a relationship shouldn't require walking every intermediate stage
// first); Archived only from Terminated, and terminal. This is a documented
// interpretation, not literal PRD text — see docs/DECISIONS.md.
// `motion` and `cadence` are free text for the same reason `segment` is on
// Partner — ADM-05's taxonomy is P1, not built. `health` is a plain
// three-value enum, not the "Enum + derived, approved values, override
// reason" formula Table 67 describes — that derivation is PORT-05 (P1,
// explicitly deferred). PORT-03 also names a `sponsor` alongside `owner` as
// a creation-time field; it's optional and ungated (no table gates
// activation or any stage on it), unlike `owner` which Table 67 gates from
// Qualified onward. `partnerId`'s own `@unique` (a Partner belongs to one
// tenant already, so this is tenant-safe without a compound key) encodes
// INV-001 ("a relationship belongs to exactly one tenant and one partner;
// duplicate active relationships require explicit program distinction") —
// Program doesn't exist yet, so no distinguishing mechanism exists either,
// meaning no duplicates at all for now.
//
// Feature: CSV Import and Partnership Activation (this migration). PRD
// IMP-02 requires "create staging batch; do not write domain objects during
// upload or mapping" — Table 12's entity list names no "staging batch"
// entity, and the one entity shaped like observable batch state (`Sync Job`
// — connection, cursor, counts, status, retry) is explicitly connector-
// shaped (its own `connection` field), not a fit for a plain file upload.
// `ImportBatch`/`ImportRow` are a direct, literal implementation of IMP-02's
// requirement text rather than an invented entity. `ImportRow.rawData`
// (the full source row as JSON) plus its `batchId` is what satisfies FLOW-A's
// acceptance criterion "every imported value retains source batch, row and
// source-column provenance" — a per-field provenance table (IMP-10's fuller
// ask, P1) is deferred; row-level is enough to answer "what did this come
// from." `matchedPartnerId`/`committedPartnerId`/`committedPartnershipId`
// are plain `String?` pointers, not Prisma `@relation`s — this is staging/
// audit-trail metadata about a pipeline run, not core relational data
// depended on for referential integrity the way `Partnership.partnerId` is.
// See docs/DECISIONS.md for the full scope cut (CSV only, not XLSX; file
// upload only, not a CRM connector; ad-hoc mapping only, not IMP-03's
// reusable saved tenant mapping; no rollback, IMP-09).
//
// Feature: Initiative, Milestone, Action, and Blocker (this migration).
// First table in the `execution` module (PRD §10.3) — Phase 3 of
// docs/ROADMAP.md. PRD Table 12 names only `Initiative` and `Action` as
// top-level entities; `Milestone` is INIT-02's child object of Initiative
// ("create ordered milestones"), not a §10.3 module boundary of its own.
// `Blocker` in the roadmap's own title is Action's own `BLOCKED` status
// plus a reason field (INIT-04: "update action status, due date, blocker,
// completion note" lists "blocker" as one of several Action FIELDS, and
// Table 13's Action state machine has `Blocked` as one of Action's own
// stages) — not a fourth entity. `Initiative.stage` and `Action.status`
// both allow a recovery move (Active⇄Blocked, In Progress⇄Blocked) that
// Table 13's own arrow-chain never draws, for the same reason documented
// on `Partnership` above. `Initiative`'s completion gate is exactly PRD
// §5.2 Golden Workflow B's stated acceptance criterion ("cannot complete
// with unresolved blocking actions unless an authorized override is
// documented") plus INIT-07's "remaining-work treatment" — completing
// requires `completionDisposition` (a scoped-down stand-in for INIT-07's
// "outcome disposition," since the real `Outcome` entity with its
// verification workflow is Phase 4, not built yet) and
// `remainingActionsTreatment`; a still-`BLOCKED` Action blocks completion
// unless `completionOverrideReason` is given (T-007, an audited override —
// only the latest is kept, same simplification as
// `Partnership.lastTransitionReason`). `successMeasure` is unshaped JSON
// for the same reason `Partner.identifiers` is — Table 67 says "Structured/
// text" without naming a schema. `Action.assigneeUserId`/
// `assigneeExternalName` are both optional but the service requires at
// least one — INIT-03/Table 67 explicitly allow "members or referenced
// counterpart owners," and no external-contact entity exists to link to
// instead. See docs/DECISIONS.md for the full scope cut (notifications,
// overdue/timeline detection, bulk update, cloning, and evidence-mandatory-
// by-action-type are all deferred).
//
// Feature: Review, Decision, and Follow-up Actions (this migration). Second
// `execution`-module feature — PRD §5.2 Golden Workflow B's middle steps and
// S08/S09. `Action.initiativeId` is now optional and `Action.reviewId` is
// added (both optional, service requires at least one) — a "follow-up
// action" recorded during a Review (FLOW-B: "review owner records decisions
// and follow-ups") need not belong to any single Initiative, so the
// existing Action entity is reused wholesale rather than inventing a
// separate "Follow-up Action" entity, the same reasoning that kept
// "Blocker" from becoming its own table. `Review`'s state machine
// (Scheduled → In Preparation → In Progress → Completed → Reopened, Table
// 13) is taken literally with no PRD-undocumented recovery move this time —
// unlike Partnership/Initiative/Action, nothing in the PRD suggests a
// "stuck" state a review needs to recover from, so the path stays strictly
// linear. `Reopened` is a real Table-13 state kept in the enum, but no
// transition reaches it yet since REV-06 ("reopen as revision") is P1.
// `Review.snapshotId` is a server-generated random id distinct from the
// review's own id, captured together with `snapshot`/`snapshotAt` on the
// Scheduled → In Preparation transition — Table 67 calls the snapshot "an
// immutable source-version set" with its own unique identifier, not just an
// embedded blob. `Decision.type` is free text (no ADM-05 taxonomy exists,
// same as `Partnership.motion`). `Decision.requiresApproval` +
// `status`/`approvedById` implement DEC-02's "route restricted decision for
// approval and enforce separation of duties" — INV-004 (approver cannot be
// the decision's own creator) is enforced in the service. See
// docs/DECISIONS.md for the full scope cut (REV-03 agenda items/templates,
// REV-06 reopen-as-revision, DEC-03 supersede — all P1/P2, deferred) and
// the RBAC reasoning (Decision's own matrix row makes Executive's "Approve"
// real for the first time, unlike Partnership/Import where it stayed
// read-only; Review borrows "Initiatives/actions" since no dedicated row
// exists for it).

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
  output   = "../generated/client"
}

// Connection URL lives in prisma.config.ts (Prisma 7) for Migrate/Studio;
// the runtime client gets its own connection via a driver adapter (src/index.ts).
datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}

enum UserStatus {
  ACTIVE
  DISABLED
}

model User {
  id              String     @id @default(uuid())
  email           String     @unique
  passwordHash    String
  name            String
  status          UserStatus @default(ACTIVE)
  emailVerifiedAt DateTime?
  createdAt       DateTime   @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime   @updatedAt

  refreshTokens                  RefreshToken[]
  passwordResetTokens            PasswordResetToken[]
  memberships                    Membership[]
  sentInvitations                Invitation[]
  partnersCreated                Partner[]               @relation("PartnerCreatedBy")
  partnersUpdated                Partner[]               @relation("PartnerUpdatedBy")
  partnershipsOwned              Partnership[]           @relation("PartnershipOwner")
  partnershipsSponsored          Partnership[]           @relation("PartnershipSponsor")
  partnershipsCreated            Partnership[]           @relation("PartnershipCreatedBy")
  partnershipsUpdated            Partnership[]           @relation("PartnershipUpdatedBy")
  importBatchesCreated           ImportBatch[]           @relation("ImportBatchCreatedBy")
  importBatchesCommitted         ImportBatch[]           @relation("ImportBatchCommittedBy")
  initiativesOwned               Initiative[]            @relation("InitiativeOwner")
  initiativesCreated             Initiative[]            @relation("InitiativeCreatedBy")
  initiativesUpdated             Initiative[]            @relation("InitiativeUpdatedBy")
  milestonesOwned                Milestone[]             @relation("MilestoneOwner")
  milestonesCreated              Milestone[]             @relation("MilestoneCreatedBy")
  milestonesUpdated              Milestone[]             @relation("MilestoneUpdatedBy")
  actionsAssigned                Action[]                @relation("ActionAssignee")
  actionsCreated                 Action[]                @relation("ActionCreatedBy")
  actionsUpdated                 Action[]                @relation("ActionUpdatedBy")
  reviewsOwned                   Review[]                @relation("ReviewOwner")
  reviewsCreated                 Review[]                @relation("ReviewCreatedBy")
  reviewsUpdated                 Review[]                @relation("ReviewUpdatedBy")
  decisionsDecided               Decision[]              @relation("DecisionDecider")
  decisionsApproved              Decision[]              @relation("DecisionApprovedBy")
  decisionsCreated               Decision[]              @relation("DecisionCreatedBy")
  decisionsUpdated               Decision[]              @relation("DecisionUpdatedBy")
  contributionsActed             Contribution[]          @relation("ContributionActor")
  contributionsCreated           Contribution[]          @relation("ContributionCreatedBy")
  contributionsUpdated           Contribution[]          @relation("ContributionUpdatedBy")
  evidenceCreated                Evidence[]              @relation("EvidenceCreatedBy")
  evidenceUpdated                Evidence[]              @relation("EvidenceUpdatedBy")
  outcomesVerified               Outcome[]               @relation("OutcomeVerifier")
  outcomesCreated                Outcome[]               @relation("OutcomeCreatedBy")
  outcomesUpdated                Outcome[]               @relation("OutcomeUpdatedBy")
  auditEvents                    AuditEvent[]
  agreementsCreated              Agreement[]             @relation("AgreementCreatedBy")
  agreementsUpdated              Agreement[]             @relation("AgreementUpdatedBy")
  agreementVersionsApproved      AgreementVersion[]      @relation("AgreementVersionApprovedBy")
  agreementVersionsCreated       AgreementVersion[]      @relation("AgreementVersionCreatedBy")
  agreementVersionsUpdated       AgreementVersion[]      @relation("AgreementVersionUpdatedBy")
  commercialRulesCreated         CommercialRule[]        @relation("CommercialRuleCreatedBy")
  commercialRulesUpdated         CommercialRule[]        @relation("CommercialRuleUpdatedBy")
  commercialRuleVersionsApproved CommercialRuleVersion[] @relation("CommercialRuleVersionApprovedBy")
  commercialRuleVersionsCreated  CommercialRuleVersion[] @relation("CommercialRuleVersionCreatedBy")
  commercialRuleVersionsUpdated  CommercialRuleVersion[] @relation("CommercialRuleVersionUpdatedBy")

  @@map("users")
}

enum TenantStatus {
  ACTIVE
  SUSPENDED
}

model Tenant {
  id        String       @id @default(uuid())
  name      String
  slug      String       @unique
  timezone  String       @default("Asia/Riyadh")
  locale    String       @default("en")
  status    TenantStatus @default(ACTIVE)
  createdAt DateTime     @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime     @updatedAt

  memberships   Membership[]
  invitations   Invitation[]
  partners      Partner[]
  partnerships  Partnership[]
  importBatches ImportBatch[]
  initiatives   Initiative[]

  @@map("tenants")
}

// PRD §2.3's MVP capability matrix columns, plus OWNER split out of ADMIN
// (see the migration note above). Ordered roughly by capability breadth —
// nothing in the code relies on enum declaration order, but it reads better.
enum MembershipRole {
  OWNER
  ADMIN
  EXECUTIVE
  MANAGER
  REVIEWER
  GUEST
}

enum MembershipStatus {
  ACTIVE
  SUSPENDED
  REMOVED
}

model Membership {
  id        String           @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId  String
  tenant    Tenant           @relation(fields: [tenantId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  userId    String
  user      User             @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  role      MembershipRole   @default(MANAGER)
  status    MembershipStatus @default(ACTIVE)
  createdAt DateTime         @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime         @updatedAt

  @@unique([tenantId, userId])
  @@index([userId])
  @@index([tenantId])
  @@map("memberships")
}

enum InvitationStatus {
  PENDING
  ACCEPTED
  REVOKED
}

// Same hash-only token storage rule as RefreshToken/PasswordResetToken.
// No DB-level uniqueness on (tenantId, email) — the service checks for an
// existing PENDING row itself, so revoking and re-inviting the same address
// doesn't fight a unique constraint on the now-superseded row.
model Invitation {
  id          String           @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId    String
  tenant      Tenant           @relation(fields: [tenantId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  email       String
  role        MembershipRole
  tokenHash   String           @unique
  invitedById String
  invitedBy   User             @relation(fields: [invitedById], references: [id])
  status      InvitationStatus @default(PENDING)
  expiresAt   DateTime
  createdAt   DateTime         @default(now())
  acceptedAt  DateTime?

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@map("invitations")
}

enum PartnerStatus {
  ACTIVE
  ARCHIVED
}

model Partner {
  id          String        @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId    String
  tenant      Tenant        @relation(fields: [tenantId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  legalName   String
  displayName String
  identifiers Json?
  segment     String?
  domains     String[]      @default([])
  status      PartnerStatus @default(ACTIVE)
  // Optimistic concurrency per PRD §4.1 — a PATCH must send the version it
  // last read; a mismatch is a 409, not a silent overwrite.
  version     Int           @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime      @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User          @relation("PartnerCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime      @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User          @relation("PartnerUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  partnership Partnership?

  // Light duplicate guard ahead of real dedup (CSV Import, Roadmap Phase 2
  // item 6, PRD FLOW-A) — two genuinely distinct partners sharing a legal
  // name within one tenant should be rare enough that this is a feature,
  // not a limitation, until that import/dedup flow exists.
  @@unique([tenantId, legalName])
  @@index([tenantId])
  @@map("partners")
}

enum PartnershipStage {
  PROSPECT
  QUALIFIED
  PLANNING
  ACTIVE
  AT_RISK
  PAUSED
  TERMINATED
  ARCHIVED
}

enum PartnershipHealth {
  HEALTHY
  NEEDS_ATTENTION
  CRITICAL
}

model Partnership {
  id        String  @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId  String
  tenant    Tenant  @relation(fields: [tenantId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  partnerId String  @unique
  partner   Partner @relation(fields: [partnerId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  stage PartnershipStage @default(PROSPECT)

  // Gated by stage, not by a NOT NULL column — see the migration note above
  // for the exact gate per field (owner from Qualified; health/nextReviewAt
  // from Active; motion/objective/cadence also required to reach Active).
  ownerId      String?
  owner        User?              @relation("PartnershipOwner", fields: [ownerId], references: [id])
  sponsorId    String?
  sponsor      User?              @relation("PartnershipSponsor", fields: [sponsorId], references: [id])
  motion       String?
  objective    String?
  cadence      String?
  health       PartnershipHealth?
  nextReviewAt DateTime?

  // PORT-04: "Transition reasons and dependencies enforced" — required by
  // the service for the exception/exit transitions (into At Risk, Paused or
  // Terminated), optional otherwise. Stores only the most recent transition's
  // reason; a full history is Audit Timeline's job (Roadmap Phase 4), not this table's.
  lastTransitionReason String?

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("PartnershipCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("PartnershipUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  initiatives   Initiative[]
  reviews       Review[]
  decisions     Decision[]
  contributions Contribution[]
  outcomes      Outcome[]
  agreements    Agreement[]

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@map("partnerships")
}

enum ImportBatchStatus {
  UPLOADED
  MAPPED
  COMMITTED
}

model ImportBatch {
  id            String            @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId      String
  tenant        Tenant            @relation(fields: [tenantId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  fileName      String
  rowCount      Int
  columnHeaders String[]
  // Target field name -> source CSV column header, e.g. {"legalName": "Company Name"}.
  fieldMapping  Json?
  status        ImportBatchStatus @default(UPLOADED)

  // Cached from the rows on every mapping recompute and on commit, so the
  // preview/results screens don't need to re-aggregate on every read.
  createdCount  Int @default(0)
  updatedCount  Int @default(0)
  skippedCount  Int @default(0)
  rejectedCount Int @default(0)

  version       Int       @default(1)
  createdAt     DateTime  @default(now())
  createdById   String
  createdBy     User      @relation("ImportBatchCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  mappedAt      DateTime?
  committedAt   DateTime?
  committedById String?
  committedBy   User?     @relation("ImportBatchCommittedBy", fields: [committedById], references: [id])

  rows ImportRow[]

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@map("import_batches")
}

enum ImportRowDisposition {
  PENDING
  CREATE
  UPDATE
  SKIP
  REJECT
}

model ImportRow {
  id        String      @id @default(uuid())
  batchId   String
  batch     ImportBatch @relation(fields: [batchId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  tenantId  String
  // 1-based, excluding the header row.
  rowNumber Int
  rawData   Json

  disposition      ImportRowDisposition @default(PENDING)
  matchReason      String?
  rejectReason     String?
  // Plain reference ids, not Prisma relations — see the migration note above.
  matchedPartnerId String?
  // User override for a SKIP row: import it anyway despite the probable-duplicate flag.
  forceCreate      Boolean              @default(false)

  committedPartnerId     String?
  committedPartnershipId String?
  committedAt            DateTime?

  @@index([batchId])
  @@index([tenantId])
  @@map("import_rows")
}

enum InitiativeStage {
  DRAFT
  PROPOSED
  APPROVED
  ACTIVE
  BLOCKED
  COMPLETED
  CANCELLED
}

enum InitiativeVisibility {
  PRIVATE
  SHAREABLE
}

enum InitiativeHealth {
  HEALTHY
  NEEDS_ATTENTION
  CRITICAL
}

enum InitiativeCompletionDisposition {
  ACHIEVED
  PARTIALLY_ACHIEVED
  NOT_ACHIEVED
}

enum RemainingActionsTreatment {
  CANCEL_REMAINING
  LEAVE_OPEN
}

model Initiative {
  id            String      @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId      String
  tenant        Tenant      @relation(fields: [tenantId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  partnershipId String
  partnership   Partnership @relation(fields: [partnershipId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  objective      String
  // {type, target, unit, date} — unshaped JSON, same reason as Partner.identifiers: Table 67
  // says "Structured/text" without naming a schema.
  successMeasure Json?
  visibility     InitiativeVisibility @default(PRIVATE)
  health         InitiativeHealth?
  ownerId        String?
  owner          User?                @relation("InitiativeOwner", fields: [ownerId], references: [id])
  startDate      DateTime?
  targetDate     DateTime?

  stage InitiativeStage @default(DRAFT)

  // Set together at completion (PATCH stage=COMPLETED) — see the migration
  // note above for why `completionDisposition` stands in for INIT-07's
  // "outcome disposition."
  completionDisposition     InitiativeCompletionDisposition?
  remainingActionsTreatment RemainingActionsTreatment?
  // T-007: completing with a still-BLOCKED action is rejected unless this is
  // set — the audited override. Only the latest is kept, same as
  // Partnership.lastTransitionReason.
  completionOverrideReason  String?
  // Optional on every stage-changing PATCH, logged into initiative_status_changed
  // — no PRD text requires it (unlike Partnership's PORT-04), so it's never enforced.
  lastTransitionReason      String?
  completedAt               DateTime?

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("InitiativeCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("InitiativeUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  milestones        Milestone[]
  actions           Action[]
  decisions         Decision[]
  contributions     Contribution[]
  outcomes          Outcome[]
  agreementVersions AgreementVersion[]

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([partnershipId])
  @@map("initiatives")
}

model Milestone {
  id           String     @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId     String
  initiativeId String
  initiative   Initiative @relation(fields: [initiativeId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  title          String
  targetDate     DateTime
  ownerId        String?
  owner          User?     @relation("MilestoneOwner", fields: [ownerId], references: [id])
  // Free text describing what "done" means for this milestone — INIT-02
  // names "completion rule" without a schema; same treatment as Partnership.cadence.
  completionRule String?
  // "Ordered milestones" (INIT-02) — display/sequence order within the initiative.
  order          Int       @default(0)
  completedAt    DateTime?

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("MilestoneCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("MilestoneUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  actions Action[]

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([initiativeId])
  @@map("milestones")
}

enum ActionStatus {
  OPEN
  IN_PROGRESS
  BLOCKED
  DONE
  CANCELLED
}

model Action {
  id           String      @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId     String
  // Both optional, but the service requires at least one — a "follow-up
  // action" recorded during a Review need not belong to any single
  // Initiative. See docs/DECISIONS.md.
  initiativeId String?
  initiative   Initiative? @relation(fields: [initiativeId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  reviewId     String?
  review       Review?     @relation(fields: [reviewId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  milestoneId  String?
  milestone    Milestone?  @relation(fields: [milestoneId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)

  title String

  // INIT-03: "members or referenced counterpart owners" — at least one of
  // these two is required (service-enforced; a DB CHECK across nullable
  // columns isn't worth the complexity for this).
  assigneeUserId       String?
  assignee             User?   @relation("ActionAssignee", fields: [assigneeUserId], references: [id])
  assigneeExternalName String?

  dueDate DateTime?
  status  ActionStatus @default(OPEN)

  // Required by the service when status transitions to BLOCKED.
  blockerReason  String?
  completionNote String?
  completedAt    DateTime?

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("ActionCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("ActionUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  contributions Contribution[]

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([initiativeId])
  @@index([reviewId])
  @@index([milestoneId])
  @@map("actions")
}

enum ReviewStage {
  SCHEDULED
  IN_PREPARATION
  IN_PROGRESS
  COMPLETED
  // Reachable per Table 13's state list, but no transition path reaches it
  // yet — REV-06 ("reopen as revision") is P1 and deferred. See docs/DECISIONS.md.
  REOPENED
}

enum ReviewNotesClassification {
  INTERNAL
  SHAREABLE
}

model Review {
  id            String      @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId      String
  partnershipId String
  partnership   Partnership @relation(fields: [partnershipId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  // Free text describing the recurring cadence this instance covers, e.g.
  // "Monthly" or "Q1 2026" — same unshaped treatment as Partnership.cadence.
  period             String?
  scheduledFor       DateTime
  ownerId            String?
  owner              User?    @relation("ReviewOwner", fields: [ownerId], references: [id])
  // Simple array, not a join table — proportionate for "who's invited."
  participantUserIds String[] @default([])

  notes               String?
  notesClassification ReviewNotesClassification @default(INTERNAL)

  // Captured server-side on Scheduled -> In Preparation (REV-02). `snapshotId`
  // is a fresh random id per capture, not the review's own id — Table 67
  // calls for a distinct, unique identifier for "an immutable source-version set."
  snapshotId String?
  snapshot   Json?
  snapshotAt DateTime?

  // Required (with the absence of any still-open linked decision/follow-up)
  // to complete — REV-05/T-008's "next cadence handling." Propagated onto
  // the parent Partnership's own `nextReviewAt` on completion.
  nextReviewAt DateTime?

  stage       ReviewStage @default(SCHEDULED)
  completedAt DateTime?

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("ReviewCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("ReviewUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  decisions Decision[]
  actions   Action[]

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([partnershipId])
  @@map("reviews")
}

enum DecisionStatus {
  RECORDED
  PENDING_APPROVAL
  APPROVED
  REJECTED
}

model Decision {
  id            String      @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId      String
  partnershipId String
  partnership   Partnership @relation(fields: [partnershipId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  reviewId      String?
  review        Review?     @relation(fields: [reviewId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)
  initiativeId  String?
  initiative    Initiative? @relation(fields: [initiativeId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)

  // Free text — no PRD taxonomy is named for decision "type" (same
  // ADM-05-not-built reason Partnership.motion stays free text).
  type          String?
  alternatives  String?
  rationale     String
  deciderId     String
  decider       User     @relation("DecisionDecider", fields: [deciderId], references: [id])
  effectiveDate DateTime
  impact        String?

  // DEC-02 / INV-004: a restricted decision needs an authorized approver who
  // is not its own creator (separation of duties) before it's final.
  requiresApproval Boolean        @default(false)
  status           DecisionStatus @default(RECORDED)
  approvedById     String?
  approvedBy       User?          @relation("DecisionApprovedBy", fields: [approvedById], references: [id])
  approvalNote     String?
  decidedAt        DateTime?

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("DecisionCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("DecisionUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([partnershipId])
  @@index([reviewId])
  @@map("decisions")
}

// Feature: Evidence, Outcome, and Verification (PRD §6.7, S11/S12, FLOW-B's
// conclusion). Table 12 names Contribution and Evidence as two distinct
// entities — Contribution is the claim of observed work ("Prove
// contribution" is S11's own stated goal); Evidence is the provenance-linked
// file/reference that backs a contribution or an outcome's verification.
//
// No literal classification taxonomy is named anywhere in the PRD (ADM-05,
// taxonomy configuration, is P1/deferred) beyond REV-04's own
// "internal/shareable classification" for review notes — reused here as the
// closest grounded precedent rather than inventing an unspecified third tier.
enum EvidenceClassification {
  INTERNAL
  SHAREABLE
}

model Contribution {
  id       String @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId String

  // EVD-01: "linked to partner, initiative, action or outcome" — "partner"
  // is read as the governed Partnership relationship, the same reading
  // every prior feature gives "the partner relationship" (Decision links
  // partnershipId, not partnerId). At least one link is required — service-
  // enforced, mirroring Action's initiativeId/reviewId pattern.
  partnershipId String?
  partnership   Partnership? @relation(fields: [partnershipId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  initiativeId  String?
  initiative    Initiative?  @relation(fields: [initiativeId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  actionId      String?
  action        Action?      @relation(fields: [actionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  outcomeId     String?
  outcome       Outcome?     @relation(fields: [outcomeId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  // No PRD-named taxonomy — same ADM-05-not-built reason Decision.type stays free text.
  type           String
  actorId        String
  actor          User                   @relation("ContributionActor", fields: [actorId], references: [id])
  observedAt     DateTime
  narrative      String
  classification EvidenceClassification @default(INTERNAL)

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("ContributionCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("ContributionUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  evidence Evidence[]

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([partnershipId])
  @@index([initiativeId])
  @@index([actionId])
  @@index([outcomeId])
  @@map("contributions")
}

model Evidence {
  id       String @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId String

  // At least one required (service-enforced) — evidence usually proves a
  // specific contribution's claim, but INV-003 needs it linkable straight to
  // an Outcome too ("cannot be Verified without at least one accessible
  // evidence record").
  contributionId String?
  contribution   Contribution? @relation(fields: [contributionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  outcomeId      String?
  outcome        Outcome?      @relation(fields: [outcomeId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  // EVD-02: "upload or reference" — source is always a free-text/URL
  // reference; storageKey/fileName/mimeType/sizeBytes/checksum are set only
  // when an actual file was uploaded; the bytes live in EvidenceFile under
  // the same storageKey (Postgres stand-in for the PRD's "files live in
  // object storage" principle — see docs/DECISIONS.md).
  source         String
  storageKey     String?
  fileName       String?
  mimeType       String?
  sizeBytes      Int?
  checksum       String?
  observedAt     DateTime
  classification EvidenceClassification @default(INTERNAL)

  // EVD-04: version/replacement chain — replacing evidence never overwrites
  // the prior material file; it creates a new row pointing back at the one
  // it replaces. `@unique` keeps the chain a simple 1:1 linked list.
  replacesEvidenceId String?   @unique
  replacesEvidence   Evidence? @relation("EvidenceReplaces", fields: [replacesEvidenceId], references: [id])
  replacedBy         Evidence? @relation("EvidenceReplaces")

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("EvidenceCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("EvidenceUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([contributionId])
  @@index([outcomeId])
  @@map("evidence")
}

// Material file bytes for Evidence, keyed by Evidence.storageKey. Kept in
// Postgres rather than on the API container's disk: the container is
// replaced on every deploy, so disk-stored files would vanish. A separate
// table keeps the bytes out of every Evidence query and lets an object
// store replace it later without touching the Evidence model. Rows are
// never updated — EVD-04 replacement writes a new key.
model EvidenceFile {
  storageKey String   @id
  tenantId   String
  content    Bytes
  createdAt  DateTime @default(now())

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@map("evidence_files")
}

// Table 13's literal chain (Draft → Submitted → Verification Required →
// Verified → Rejected → Superseded) is read as a reachability list, not a
// strict sequence — OUT-03 requires a verifier to take three different
// actions from Submitted (verify/reject/request more evidence), and
// VERIFICATION_REQUIRED needs a documented recovery move back to SUBMITTED
// once more evidence is attached, the same "stuck state" pattern applied to
// every other state machine in this codebase. SUPERSEDED is reachable per
// the state list but no transition path reaches it — OUT-04 ("supersede a
// verified outcome") is P1 and deferred, same treatment as ReviewStage's
// unreachable REOPENED.
enum OutcomeStatus {
  DRAFT
  SUBMITTED
  VERIFICATION_REQUIRED
  VERIFIED
  REJECTED
  SUPERSEDED
}

model Outcome {
  id            String      @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId      String
  partnershipId String
  partnership   Partnership @relation(fields: [partnershipId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  initiativeId  String?
  initiative    Initiative? @relation(fields: [initiativeId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)

  // No PRD-named taxonomy for "type" — free text, same reason Decision.type is.
  type          String
  claimedResult String
  value         Decimal? @db.Decimal(18, 4)
  unit          String?
  period        String?

  status OutcomeStatus @default(DRAFT)

  // OUT-02: submitted to an authorized verifier — required to reach
  // Submitted; INV-003/DEC-02-style separation of duties (T-010) blocks the
  // outcome's own creator from being its verifier.
  verifierId          String?
  verifier            User?     @relation("OutcomeVerifier", fields: [verifierId], references: [id])
  submittedAt         DateTime?
  verifiedAt          DateTime?
  verifierDisposition String?
  rejectionReason     String?

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("OutcomeCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("OutcomeUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  contributions Contribution[]
  evidence      Evidence[]

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([partnershipId])
  @@index([initiativeId])
  @@index([verifierId])
  @@map("outcomes")
}

// Opaque, rotated on every use (old one revoked when a new one is issued).
// Only the SHA-256 hash is stored — the raw token exists only in the client's
// httpOnly cookie and is never persisted or logged.
model RefreshToken {
  id        String    @id @default(uuid())
  userId    String
  user      User      @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  tokenHash String    @unique
  expiresAt DateTime
  createdAt DateTime  @default(now())
  revokedAt DateTime?

  @@index([userId])
  @@map("refresh_tokens")
}

// Same hash-only storage rule as RefreshToken. Single-use — `usedAt` is set
// the moment it's redeemed and the token is rejected on any later attempt.
model PasswordResetToken {
  id        String    @id @default(uuid())
  userId    String
  user      User      @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  tokenHash String    @unique
  expiresAt DateTime
  createdAt DateTime  @default(now())
  usedAt    DateTime?

  @@index([userId])
  @@map("password_reset_tokens")
}

// Feature: Audit Timeline and Audit Search (PRD §6.11, S16, AUD-01/02).
// Append-only — no update/delete path is ever exposed; PRD §4.4's own text
// says so explicitly ("Audit events are append-only"), and Table 13 lists no
// state machine for it because there's no lifecycle to enforce. Written by
// `recordAuditEvent()` (`modules/audit-operations/audit.service.ts`) as a
// plain function every domain service calls directly after a material
// mutation — not through NestJS DI, the same "singleton import, not
// constructor-injected" pattern `prisma` itself already uses everywhere in
// this codebase — so adding an audit call never changes a service's
// constructor signature or breaks its existing unit tests.
model AuditEvent {
  id       String  @id @default(uuid())
  // Plain scalar, not a `Tenant` relation — the same lighter shape every
  // other tenant-scoped-but-not-tenant-owned entity already uses (Review,
  // Decision, Action, Contribution, Evidence, Outcome all carry `tenantId`
  // without a Prisma-level FK to `Tenant`), appropriate here since
  // AuditEvent is written by every module, not owned by one root entity.
  tenantId String
  actorId  String?
  actor    User?   @relation(fields: [actorId], references: [id])

  // e.g. "partnership_created", "outcome_verified" — reuses the literal
  // names already chosen for this codebase's existing analytics-event
  // Logger lines wherever one already exists (see docs/DECISIONS.md), so
  // the audit trail and the console analytics log for the same mutation
  // are searchable by the same string.
  action     String
  objectType String
  objectId   String

  // Table 67: "Encrypted JSON" — no field-level encryption-at-rest layer
  // exists anywhere in this codebase yet (same category of infra gap as
  // "no object storage integration" for Evidence files); stored as plain
  // Prisma `Json` and documented as a deferred hardening step, not silently
  // dropped or faked.
  before Json?
  after  Json?

  // Table 67: "a correlation id" — defaults to a fresh id per event
  // (self-correlating) rather than the HTTP request's own `x-correlation-id`
  // header, since threading that header through every already-built
  // service's method signature would be a much larger retrofit than this
  // phase's scope justifies; still a real, filterable column per AUD-02.
  correlationId String   @default(uuid())
  createdAt     DateTime @default(now())

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([objectType, objectId])
  @@index([actorId])
  @@index([correlationId])
  @@index([createdAt])
  @@map("audit_events")
}

// Feature: Agreements and Commercial Rules (v2, PRD §6.8, S10, AGR-01/02/
// 04/05, RULE-01–04) — the load-bearing prerequisite for the Revenue-Share
// Pack's Partner Claim (CLM-02 requires every claim link "one partner,
// revenue event and applicable agreement/rule").
//
// Both Agreement and CommercialRule follow the same two-tier shape: a
// parent with a stable identity referenced everywhere downstream, and
// child *Version rows carrying the actual effective-dated, approved
// content — Table 67 names "Agreement Version" as its own row with its
// own `effective_from/to` field distinct from the parent, and INV-002
// ("An effective agreement/rule version cannot be edited; corrections
// create a superseding version") names "agreement/rule version" as one
// parallel concept applied to both families. A version is immutable once
// `APPROVED` — corrections are a new version, never an edit, the same
// "preserve, don't overwrite" discipline Evidence's own replacement chain
// (EVD-04) already established.
enum AgreementStatus {
  CAPTURED
  IN_REVIEW
  EFFECTIVE
  // Reachable once a later version is approved while an earlier one is
  // Effective — Table 13's own chain names this as the state after
  // Effective, not a loop back to it.
  AMENDED
  SUSPENDED
  EXPIRED
  TERMINATED
}

enum ApprovalStatus {
  DRAFT
  APPROVED
}

model Agreement {
  id            String          @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId      String
  partnershipId String
  partnership   Partnership     @relation(fields: [partnershipId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  // AGR-01: "link source document/reference" — a URL/free-text reference,
  // not a stored file; no object storage integration exists yet, the same
  // gap Evidence's own file handling already documents.
  sourceRef     String?
  status        AgreementStatus @default(CAPTURED)

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("AgreementCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("AgreementUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  versions AgreementVersion[]

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([partnershipId])
  @@map("agreements")
}

model AgreementVersion {
  id           String      @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId     String
  agreementId  String
  agreement    Agreement   @relation(fields: [agreementId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  // AGR-04: "link agreement/rule versions to relationship, initiative and
  // claim" — the relationship link is the parent Agreement's own
  // partnershipId; this is the version-specific, optional Initiative
  // scoping, the same optional-link pattern Decision/Contribution use.
  // The Claim link is added from Claim's own side once that entity exists.
  initiativeId String?
  initiative   Initiative? @relation(fields: [initiativeId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)

  versionNumber  Int
  terms          String?
  effectiveFrom  DateTime
  // Open-ended (ongoing) when null.
  effectiveTo    DateTime?
  approvalStatus ApprovalStatus @default(DRAFT)
  approvedById   String?
  approvedBy     User?          @relation("AgreementVersionApprovedBy", fields: [approvedById], references: [id])
  approvedAt     DateTime?

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("AgreementVersionCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("AgreementVersionUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([agreementId])
  @@map("agreement_versions")
}

// Table 12: "type, conditions, precedence, effective dates, version" — no
// partnership/relationship field is named, unlike every other domain
// entity in this codebase; a Commercial Rule is tenant-wide reusable
// eligibility/attribution logic, not owned by one governed relationship.
// Table 13 names no independent state machine for it either (only
// Agreement's own row exists there) — RULE-03's literal text ("approve
// effective-dated immutable rule version") is the only lifecycle text,
// and it describes the *version*, not a parent-level chain — so, unlike
// Agreement, CommercialRule itself carries no status field of its own.
enum CommercialRuleType {
  ELIGIBILITY
  ATTRIBUTION
}

model CommercialRule {
  id       String             @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId String
  name     String
  type     CommercialRuleType

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("CommercialRuleCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("CommercialRuleUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  versions CommercialRuleVersion[]

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@map("commercial_rules")
}

model CommercialRuleVersion {
  id               String         @id @default(uuid())
  tenantId         String
  commercialRuleId String
  commercialRule   CommercialRule @relation(fields: [commercialRuleId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  versionNumber Int
  // Resolves which rule applies when more than one could match — the
  // actual selection logic is Partner Claim's job (v2 item 14, not yet
  // built); this phase only stores and orders by it.
  precedence    Int       @default(0)
  // RULE-01: "approved condition/operator catalog" — a small, fixed,
  // explainable DSL evaluated server-side, deliberately not arbitrary
  // code, so RULE-04's "explain rule evaluation as inputs, conditions,
  // result and version" stays reproducible and safe. Shape:
  // { combinator: 'AND' | 'OR', conditions: [{ field, operator, value }] }.
  definition    Json
  effectiveFrom DateTime
  effectiveTo   DateTime?

  approvalStatus ApprovalStatus @default(DRAFT)
  approvedById   String?
  approvedBy     User?          @relation("CommercialRuleVersionApprovedBy", fields: [approvedById], references: [id])
  approvedAt     DateTime?

  // RULE-02: "test rule against historical/sample events before approval
  // ... test results stored with version." No real Revenue Event exists
  // yet (v2 item 14) to test against historical records, so this stores
  // the results of user-supplied sample cases instead — documented in
  // docs/DECISIONS.md as a scope simplification, not a silent gap.
  testResults Json?

  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("CommercialRuleVersionCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
  updatedById String
  updatedBy   User     @relation("CommercialRuleVersionUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([commercialRuleId])
  @@map("commercial_rule_versions")
}
